// Bars 5:2:5; triangle depth 1.9125 of 3 is 306 of 480 in the Commons drawing (derived).
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Demisexual Pride Flag"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  source "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Demisexual_Pride_Flag.svg"
  source "https://aceweek.org/stories/ace-flag-history"
  source "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demisexuality"
  note "No designer or first publication was found. Ace Week says the exact origins of the demisexual flag are unknown and that it may have been proposed like the gray-asexual flag, by an upload to Wikipedia. Searches found conflicting unsupported claims (an AVEN user in 2010, a 2006 Tumblr user), and none was verified. This file is written from the Commons drawing, which credits Vimopu with the original image in 2013 and calls it a claimed flag."
  note "Meanings, per Wikipedia citing Old Dominion University: black triangle for asexuality, gray for gray asexuality, white for sexuality, purple for community."
  note "Bars 5:2:5, the triangle's depth, the 3:5 proportion and all four colors (#ffffff, #6e0070, #d2d2d2, #000000) are the Commons drawing's (viewBox 800 by 480; stripes 200, 80, 200; triangle apex at x=306). No other source states them."
}
palette {
  white "#ffffff"
  purple "#6e0070"
  grey "#d2d2d2"
  black "#000000"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars white purple grey {
  ratio 5 2 5
}

chevrons black {
  depth 1.9125
}
